        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00090:alt:fig-00006-alt",
          "text": "A reaction mechanism shows 2-bromo-3-fluoro-3-methylbutane reacts with antimony pentafluoride in the presence of liquid sulfur dioxide to form bromonium ion (stable in sulfur dioxide solution)."
